2026-02-20T03:57:15.278698Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019c7930-7929-7e03-861e-f8e1d1dc563d}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"cat <<'EOF' > .specify/memory/constitution.md\n<!--\nSync Impact Report\n- Version change: 0.0.0 (template) -> 1.0.0\n- Modified principles: N/A (new principles defined)\n- Added sections: Core Principles, Quality Gates, Development Workflow, Governance\n- Removed sections: None\n- Templates requiring updates:\n  - .specify/templates/plan-template.md: ✅ updated\n  - .specify/templates/spec-template.md: ✅ updated\n  - .specify/templates/tasks-template.md: ✅ updated\n- Follow-up TODOs:\n  - TODO(RATIFICATION_DATE): original adoption date unknown\n-->\n# Specify Sample Constitution\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Code Quality & Maintainability\nAll changes MUST pass linting, formatting, and static analysis with zero warnings.\nPublic APIs MUST be documented with clear usage examples where applicable.\nError handling MUST be explicit and observable; silent failures are not allowed.\nDuplicated logic MUST be refactored or explicitly justified in the PR.\n\n### II. Testing Standards (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\nEvery behavior change MUST include tests that cover the new or modified behavior.\nBug fixes MUST include a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after.\nTests MUST run in CI and remain deterministic; flaky tests are treated as failures.\nTest scope MUST match risk: unit tests for logic, integration tests for boundaries.\n\n### III. UX Consistency & Accessibility\nUI changes MUST use approved design system components, tokens, and patterns.\nAny deviation from the design system MUST be documented and approved in review.\nNew or modified UI MUST meet WCAG 2.1 AA for keyboard, contrast, and labels.\nUser-facing copy MUST follow the project style guide and terminology.\n\n### IV. Performance Budgets & Validation\nEach feature MUST define measurable performance budgets in the plan (e.g., latency,\nthroughput, memory, bundle size, or frame rate).\nChanges MUST include benchmark or profiling evidence that budgets are met.\nRegressions beyond budget require remediation or explicit approval with a plan.\n\n### V. Change Safety & Review Discipline\nAll changes MUST be code-reviewed before merge; high-risk changes require two\napprovals or a designated reviewer.\nCI MUST be green for lint, tests, and performance checks prior to merge.\nBreaking changes MUST include a migration plan and versioning update.\n\n## Quality Gates\n\n- Lint/format/static analysis pass with zero warnings\n- Required tests added and CI green\n- UX consistency review completed for UI changes\n- Performance budgets defined and validated\n- Any exception MUST be documented with explicit reviewer approval\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n- Features require a spec and plan before implementation begins\n- Work is delivered in small, reviewable increments with clear rollback paths\n- Documentation MUST be updated for public APIs and user-facing changes\n- Release notes MUST capture breaking changes and performance impacts\n\n## Governance\n\n- This constitution supersedes all other development guidance\n- Amendments require documentation, rationale, and version update\n- Versioning follows semantic versioning for governance changes\n- Compliance is reviewed in every PR and release checklist\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: TODO(RATIFICATION_DATE): original adoption date unknown | **Last Amended**: 2026-02-20\nEOF"} thread_id=019c7930-7929-7e03-861e-f8e1d1dc563d
